From 4c2f8be182e2ea5c6d17f58959d9490cef5c4c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 11:47:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] perf: shrink per-effect/atom/computed retained memory

- ReactiveEffect.deps starts as a shared empty sentinel; the first tracked
  dep swaps in a capacity-1 [dep] literal via addDep (push on an empty
  array made V8 pre-grow the elements store to capacity 17, wasting 64B
  on every single-dep binding effect; effects that never track pay zero)
- primitive atom updater becomes a named function expression: the
  self-reference no longer captures a closure variable, so each atom
  drops its private Context object (~20B per atom)
- Computed constructor stops using parameter properties for optional
  args (applyPatch/callbacks/skipIndicator/preventEffectSession are
  assigned only when provided; defaults live on the prototype)

measure-retained (node --expose-gc, retained bytes per object):
atom 176->136B, atom+1 subscriber 620->452B, light effect 136->104B,
computed(atom dep) 946->707B, bare computed 490->388B, RxList(empty)
274->226B. measure-speed hot paths equal or faster (in-process A/B);
all 207 tests pass.
---
 src/atom.ts           | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 src/computed.ts       | 24 +++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/notify.ts         |  4 ++--
 src/reactiveEffect.ts | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

